  "name": null,
  "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"160px\" align=\"center\">$2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td><td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"160px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
